# rsc harness / AI tooling — local only, never committed.
# Git tracks the code project only; nothing of the harness goes in.
#
# No trailing slash: these paths may be real directories OR symlinks into a
# synced store (Google Drive: "Mi unidad/andbench-harness/"). A trailing slash
# matches directories only, so a symlink of the same name would leak into git —
# matching both forms keeps the harness ignored regardless of layout.
# Root-anchored (leading "/") so a product file of the same basename deeper in
# the tree (e.g. docs/AGENTS.md) stays trackable.
/.claude
/.codex
/.rsc
/01-TOOLS
/02-DOCS
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Tooling caches
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# Local env / secrets
.env
*.local

# Private dataset split — custodied out of the repo (anti-contamination §3)
/data/private/

# Reproduction run artifacts (regenerated by scripts/reproduce.sh; a run also
# writes a private split, which must never be committed — see P11).
/runs/
